/* The complete OpenGL 3.3 core API, one function per line, alphabetical (the Khronos registry's gl:core=3.3 set, as in
 * GLAD 2.0.8's gl.h). gl.c expands this table into the GL module's wrappers, their registration and the loader.
 *
 *   GL_FUNCTION(return type, name, "Traditional Chinese alias", (parameter types), "argument kinds")
 *   GL_VOID(name, "Traditional Chinese alias", (parameter types), "argument kinds")      functions returning void
 *
 * Argument kinds, one per parameter, say what a script passes (the C type decides the binary conversion):
 *   n   a number (integral and in range for integer types; GLboolean also takes true/false, 64-bit types GL_INTEGER64)
 *   p   a pointer: GL_DATA, GL_POINTER, 0 or null, an array of the pointed-to type (copied back when the type is not
 *       const), a string for GLchar text, an array of strings for GLchar lists
 *   o   a pointer that may also be a nonnegative byte offset into the bound buffer (vertex attributes, indices)
 *   c   the element count of the arguments marked with a multiplier
 * A pointer kind followed by a number must hold count x number elements of its type ("c p1" for glGenBuffers,
 * "n c n p16" for glUniformMatrix4fv): arrays need that many elements and GL_DATA that many bytes of the type.
 */
